# Business Case – Patient Appointment No-Show Reduction

## 1. Executive Summary

The hospital manages a large number of outpatient appointments. A percentage of patients do not attend their scheduled appointments without cancelling or rescheduling in advance.

This results in unused appointment slots, reduced doctor utilization, additional administrative work, and potential revenue loss.

This project proposes a solution to improve appointment attendance through automated reminders, appointment confirmation, easy rescheduling, cancellation tracking, and management reporting.

## 2. Business Problem

The current appointment management process has several challenges:

* Patients may forget their appointments.
* Patients may not receive timely reminders.
* Rescheduling an appointment may require manual staff assistance.
* Cancellation reasons are not consistently captured.
* Staff may need to manually follow up with patients.
* Management has limited visibility into no-show patterns.

## 3. Business Objective

The primary objective is to reduce patient appointment no-shows and improve utilization of available appointment slots.

### Target

The proposed solution aims to achieve a **20% reduction in the no-show rate within six months of implementation**.

> Note: This is a proposed project target for portfolio purposes, not a claim about an actual hospital implementation.

## 4. Proposed Solution

The proposed solution will provide:

1. Automated appointment reminders.
2. Appointment confirmation functionality.
3. Appointment rescheduling functionality.
4. Appointment cancellation functionality.
5. Cancellation reason tracking.
6. Staff visibility into unconfirmed appointments.
7. Management reporting and analytics.

